      "sha": "b9018ae981a07071a4a71c49647fade236636532",
      "message": "feat(sdk): add getSelectedText() API, Editor container pass-through props and onReady callback\n\nImplements two P0 roadmap items for SDK API completeness:\n\n1. core: add `getSelectedText(): string` to EditorAPI — returns the text\n   within the current selection range, or \"\" when collapsed.\n\n2. react + vue: `<Editor />` now forwards HTML div attributes (className,\n   style, data-*, aria-*) to the container element and accepts an `onReady`\n   callback that fires once with the EditorAPI after initialization.\n\n   - React: filter known editor config keys via EDITOR_PROP_KEYS set,\n     spread remainder onto container div; onReady fires via useEffect.\n   - Vue: declare all editor config props so Vue strips them from $attrs;\n     fallthrough attrs (class, style, data-*) land on the root div\n     automatically; onReady fires via watch(editor, { immediate: true }).\n\nBoth bindings share matching semantics and include new tests covering\ncontainer attribute forwarding, onReady callback, and getSelectedText\nwith empty, forward, and reversed selections.\n\nCloses roadmap items #4 and #5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "date": "2026-06-03T07:40:28Z"
    },
    {
